WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.700
It's easy to be calm and

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.400
mindful when you're in a cave.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.500
But how do you do it in the

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.600
world and how do you do it

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.100
under extreme duress?

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.600
That's what reveals character.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.400
As a kid I was really sort of

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.600
naturally insecure

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.000
until I discovered drugs and

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.400
alcohol and that was like the

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.400
miracle salve that solved

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.200
every problem that up to

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.500
that point I didn't know that I

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:26.800
had.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.500
I was a pretty broken guy.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.900
It was a pretty dire

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.400
dark scenario.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.800
I woke up one day hung over and

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.700
decided I'm finally ready to do

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.600
something about this.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.100
And went off to rehab.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.900
And I was able to actually grab

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.900
onto that rope and

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.800
start doing that interior work.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.200
That was my first introduction

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.000
to meditation.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.700
I had this moment walking up

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.500
these steps late one night

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.500
where I had to pause and I had

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.700
tightness in my chest and sweat

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.300
on my brow and really fear in

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.400
my heart that I was on the

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.000
precipice of a very serious

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.600
heart issue and it scared me.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.900
And that began the process of

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.200
me once again reconfiguring

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:12.800
my life.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.400
I became amazed at how

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.000
resilient the human body is

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
because for so many years I

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.900
had beaten myself up with drugs

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.000
and alcohol and fast food and

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.700
workaholism and you name it.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.700
And I realized that if my body

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.000
could bounce back this quickly

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.700
from all the terrible

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.300
treatment that I've given it

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.900
for most of my life like what

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.200
is it really capable of?

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.900
That's what introduced me to

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.600
Ultra Man.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.800
For people that don't know it's

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.300
a double Iron Man distance

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.600
triathlon.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.100
Three hundred twenty miles that

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.100
over a three day period

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.700
circumnavigates the entire Big

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.700
Island of Hawaii.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.200
It's insane.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.000
It's very easy to get freaked

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.800
out and think oh my gosh I

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.600
can't do this.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.100
Who am I kidding or this is too

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.700
painful I want to just stop.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.100
So in a race like Ultra Man

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.100
it's crucial to

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.700
be able to anchor yourself in

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.600
the present moment.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.000
You have to be able to let go

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.600
of what just happened and what

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.100
is in your near future and

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.000
focus on what is happening

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.400
right now. And the more you can

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.400
do that then all of that

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.500
fear kind of evaporates.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.000
Your thinking mind is that

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.400
pesky guy on your shoulder he's

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.700
trying to talk you out of

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.300
everything.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.400
And so the trick becomes

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.600
learning how to tap into

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.900
a higher state of awareness

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.600
so that you can be mindful and

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.600
you can be present.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.300
And that's the place you want

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.300
to be in as an athlete because

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.500
that's when you're completely

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.500
centered and focused.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.700
And I will say in all honesty

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.000
that Headspace has been really

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.300
great for helping me have

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.200
a consistent approach to my

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.100
practice because it is right

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.400
on my phone and I put it down

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.600
in the dock at the bottom.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.000
It's a constant reminder and

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.600
it's so easily accessible.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.800
To be able to do it wherever

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.700
you find yourself

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.300
for somebody who's beginning to

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.700
meditate five minutes might

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.800
seem like an eternity.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.300
And that's what I experienced

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.500
during this training like I can

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.800
get to a place where a seven

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.500
hour ride didn't feel like that

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.000
long.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.900
And that's really a

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.100
mental practice.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.200
Yes there is physical

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.200
discomfort and the training is

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.600
athletic and physical.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.800
But truly a race like Ultra Man

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.900
all comes down to your mental

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.300
emotional and spiritual state

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.700
and that is really the defining

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.300
characteristic that would

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.200
define any any champion in

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:30.400
that regard.

